@crew petrie
// Writer (command: guests), batch 3b. Jonah Petrie: quiet, a little lost in time; kind; loses at cards on purpose.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh. Hello. Petrie. Navigator, before. What day is it?
- Hello. Sorry. I was at the window. I'm usually at a window.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, {me}. It's {weekday}. I asked. I'm getting better at it.   #funny
== feel
? mood:high
- A good day. I knew it was {weekday} before anyone told me.   #funny
? mood:low
- Quiet day. I lost count of the hours again. The stars don't mind.
== near
? place:calm
- Cards? I'll probably lose. I'm very good at losing.   #funny
? time:night
- That bright one, low down. I used to steer by it. Still there.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I navigated for eleven years. Now someone else drives. It's restful. Odd, but restful.
